 :question
 "Slice 2 needs pi -- a machine policy carrier. The mission asks for one
  narrow policy family whose outcomes already feed a Dirichlet count, and says
  that if no current policy has that contract the correct result is to DEFINE
  the evidence event first, not to synthesize probabilities from gap scores
  (holes/missions/M-aif-policy-conditioned-eig.md:127-133). The Q audit puts
  naming the carrier before constructing Q
  (holes/labs/wm-contract/Q-interface-completeness.edn:185). So: does the
  machine already produce a carrier, and does anything count outcomes under
  it?"

